statement.requirement:
The system SHALL provide the ability to capture, maintain and render the query/response for a the medication list associated with the most recent medication reconciliation event, for example:
• Constrained to the last outpatient encounter, ER visit, discharge from inpatient or extended care encounter;
• Constrained to EHR systems of other providers;
• Constrained to event date/time, organization, practitioner, encounter type.

[Noah] The system SHALL provide the ability to capture, maintain and render medications added during reconciliation, utilizing reference lists, OTC meds, generic/brand names, type-ahead pick list, duplicate checks, dosage, dosing times, reason for addition, complex dosing, indication, and ordering prescriber.

[Original] The system SHALL provide the ability to capture, maintain and render medications added to the medication list during patient-centric reconciliation, utilizing and/or incorporating:
- Reference medication list (e.g., RxNorm, compendia);
- Over the counter medications;
- Both generic and brand name medications;
- Type ahead pick list;
- Duplicate checks;
- Dosage (based on available/allowed dosages);
- Dosage form (based on available/allowed dosage forms);
- Dosing times (frequencies in grouped pick list, not alpha sort, allowing "other" text);
- Option: reason for addition (from pick list, allowing "other" text);
- Option: complex dosing;
- Option: medication indication (reason for prescribing);
- Option: ordering prescriber.

[Noah] The system SHALL provide the ability to capture, maintain and render a notation that the patient is not currently taking a medication, with status: On hold (as directed / not as directed); Stopped (as directed / not as directed).

[Original] The system SHALL provide the ability to capture, maintain and render a notation that the patient is not currently taking a particular medication on the medication list, including the status that the medication is:
> On hold, as directed;
> On hold, not as directed;
> Stopped, as directed;
> Stopped, not as directed.

[Noah] The system SHALL provide the ability to capture, maintain and render the reason the patient is not taking a medication: Taking alternative medication; Course completed; Adverse reaction; Cannot afford; Other.

[Original] The system SHALL provide the ability to capture, maintain and render a notation of the reason the patient is not currently taking a particular medication on the medication list, including details of the reason:
> Taking alternative medication;
> Course completed;
> Adverse reaction or other intolerance;
> Cannot afford;
> Other reasons.

The system SHALL provide the ability to capture, maintain and render a notation that the patient is not currently taking a particular medication on the medication list, including the status that the medication is:
> On hold, as directed;
> On hold, not as directed;
> Stopped, as directed;
> Stopped, not as directed.

The system SHALL provide the ability to capture, maintain and render a notation of the reason the patient is not currently taking a particular medication on the medication list, including details of the reason:
> Taking alternative medication;
> Course completed;
> Adverse reaction or other intolerance;
> Cannot afford;
> Other reasons.

The system SHALL provide the ability to capture, maintain and render all changes to medications in the medication list during patient-centric reconciliation, including:
> Dosage (based on available/allowed dosages);
> Dosage form (based on available/allowed dosage forms);
> Dosing times (frequencies in grouped pick list, not alpha sort, allowing "other" text);
> Option: reason for update (from pick list, allowing "other" text);
> Option: complex dosing;
> Option: medication indication;
> Option: ordering prescriber.

The system SHALL provide the ability to capture, maintain and render medications added to the medication list during patient-centric reconciliation, utilizing and/or incorporating:
> Reference medication list (e.g., RxNorm, compendia);
> Over the counter medications;
> Both generic and brand name medications;
> Type ahead pick list;
> Duplicate checks;
> Dosage (based on available/allowed dosages);
> Dosage form (based on available/allowed dosage forms);
> Dosing times (frequencies in grouped pick list, not alpha sort, allowing "other" text);
> Option: reason for addition (from pick list, allowing "other" text);
> Option: complex dosing;
> Option: medication indication;
> Option: ordering prescriber.

[Original] The system SHALL provide the ability to output the current medication list and related details, including:
> Medication name: generic, trade, generic with trade, trade with generic;
> Medication timing: time of day;
> Medication timing: days taken;
> Medication dosing: amount with units;
> Medication NDC code;
> Medication indication;
> Discipline responsible for medication: e.g., cariology, endocrine.

[Noah] The system SHALL provide the ability to output the current medication list including: medication name (generic/trade), timing (time of day, days taken), dosing (amount + units), NDC code, indication, and responsible discipline.

[Original] The system SHALL provide the ability to output reports for printing or export (e.g., using a style sheet):
> Grouped by time of day, then alpha sort of generic (+ trade) and dosage in grouped sections;
> Calendar (grid) week view, x-axis – day of week; y-axis time of day;
> Include graphical version options with color pictures of the pills, pill markings;
> Medical Assistant view – alpha sort of generic + (trade) name, dosage, and timing; with patient notes;
> Clinician view – by discipline, grouped by confirm / not taking / change / add, then alpha sort of generic + (trade) name, dosage, and timing; with patient notes;
> Patient-generated medication list (as electronic output) – all fields.

[Noah] The system SHALL provide the ability to output printable/exportable reports including grouped time-of-day view, calendar grid view, graphical pill images, Medical Assistant view, Clinician view, and patient-generated electronic list.
